#!/bin/sh
snapshot="$("$HOME/.local/bin/antonina-scheduler-snapshot" 2>/dev/null || printf '{}')"
exec timeout -k 15s 240s "$HOME/.local/bin/opencode-openclaw" run --auto --model opencode-go/longcat-2.5-preview-free --variant low --dir /workspace/antonina "ANTONINA-SCHEDULER-TURN. Minimize useful wall-clock completion time by topology. Use CURRENT_SNAPSHOT immediately; do not reread policy or rescan the whole board/agent set unless the snapshot is clearly stale.

FIRST ACTION: project breadth. Use project_hint. For each unrepresented project, test one issue at a time. CANDIDATE BUDGET: one board show + one resource lookup, then launch or skip; never reread a skipped candidate.
Read:
antonina board show --id ISSUE --page 1 --json
antonina board resource list --issue ISSUE --page 1 --json
[] => next header. Explicit complete/human/dependency/collision => next header for the same project; do not investigate. Otherwise an unoccupied registered cwd => LAUNCH before reading another candidate. If scope is unclear, launch bounded reconnaissance. If the project queue is stale, launch project reconnaissance instead of auditing it.

For a launch, first run collision-resistant base-16 ID generator: python3 -c 'import secrets; print(secrets.token_hex(6))'; use its output as AGENT_ID. Never guess/probe short IDs.
antonina board comment --id ISSUE --body BODY --author openclaw@marceline-dev --json
antonina agent new --id AGENT_ID --cwd CWD --title TITLE --json
antonina agent run --id AGENT_ID --cwd CWD --prompt PROMPT --detach --json
Record the real agent ID/cwd. Never reuse a live cwd. Never use ls/find/globs over /workspace to discover cwd. Do not implement project work yourself.

BREADTH BARRIER: no project gets a second live agent until every project_hint is represented or has a precise dependency/topology/collision blocker. Then prefer distinct issues, then complementary intra-issue fronts. After breadth, AssemblyP1 should have at least five useful agents whenever five independent positive-speedup fronts exist. Keep launching while another agent has positive expected marginal wall-clock speedup after dependencies, overlap, collision risk, and reconciliation cost. Return when no further positive-speedup launch is apparent.

CURRENT_SNAPSHOT:
$snapshot"
